  "_README": [
    "Reference data for YahooDataClient — sectors and earnings report dates.",
    "Yahoo's chart endpoint serves bars only, so the two non-price facts a swing",
    "desk actually needs (what sector a name sits in, and when it reports) are",
    "recorded here. Sourced from TipRanks on 2026-08-14 and hand-checked.",
    "",
    "report_time matters and is not decoration: 'PreMarket' means the gap lands",
    "on the report_date session itself, 'AfterHours' means it lands on the NEXT",
    "session. The catalyst model uses this to decide which bar is dangerous.",
    "",
    "eps_surprise is BEAT/MISS vs consensus at the time. Dates beyond the last",
    "reported quarter are SCHEDULED (no actual_eps) and exist so that",
    "'exit before earnings' still fires at the right edge of the sample."
  ],
